---
layout: layouts/base.njk
schemaType: WebPage
title: AI Training for Agrifood Teams
metaTitle: "AI Training for Agriculture & Agrifood Teams | Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko"
description: AI literacy and AI fluency training for agriculture and agrifood organisations — lectures, workshops, multi-session courses and custom programmes by Dr. Maryna Kuzmenko.
---
{#
  Training for organisations. Every list on this page — levels, formats,
  add-ons, topics, audiences, steps, outcomes and questions — is read from
  _data/training.js, which mirrors the offer published at
  aiinagriculture.org/ai-training-agrifood/. Change the words there, not here.
  No prices on this page: every format is quoted.
#}
{% from "partials/photo.njk" import photo %}
{% set awareness = training.courses.awareness %}
{% set fluency = training.courses.fluency %}

<section class="hero">
  <span class="eyebrow">Training for agriculture and agrifood</span>
  <h1>AI fluency for the people who <span class="italic-text">grow, process and feed the world.</span></h1>
  <p class="lead" style="max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto 30px;">
    Practical AI literacy training for agricultural and agrifood organisations. From a one-hour
    lecture to a fully customised course, your team learns what AI can really do in the field, the
    lab and the supply chain, and how to use it with confidence.
  </p>
  <div class="hero__actions">
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ training.enquiry }}">Book a training session</a>
    <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#topics">Explore topics</a>
  </div>

  <div class="stats training-glance">
    <div class="stat"><strong>45 min – 12 wks</strong><span>From a keynote to a full course</span></div>
    <div class="stat"><strong>Online or on site</strong><span>Live, in person, or both</span></div>
    <div class="stat"><strong>5 to hundreds</strong><span>Workshops of up to 25 per group</span></div>
    <div class="stat"><strong>No coding</strong><span>Advanced tracks on request</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <span class="eyebrow">Why AI fluency, why now</span>
  <h2>AI is already in your sector. Is your team ready for it?</h2>
  <p class="lead" style="max-width: 820px;">
    Computer vision counts fruit and measures leaves. Sensors and models predict yield, disease and
    milk output. Language tools draft reports, grant bids and supplier emails in seconds. Yet most
    teams were never taught what AI actually is, where it works and where it fails — which leads to
    two costly mistakes: ignoring tools that could save hours every week, or buying solutions that
    never fit the farm, the lab or the data.
  </p>
  <p style="max-width: 820px; color: var(--muted);">{{ training.definition }}</p>

  <div class="grid training-levels">
    {% for level in training.levels %}
      <div class="card card--compact">
        <span class="eyebrow" style="font-size: 10px;">Level {{ loop.index }}</span>
        <h3>{{ level.name }}</h3>
        <p>{{ level.meaning }}</p>
        <p class="training-levels__route">{{ level.route }}</p>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  <span class="eyebrow">Who it is for</span>
  <h2>Built for agriculture and agrifood teams</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    {% for audience in training.audiences %}
      <div class="card card--compact">
        <h3>{{ audience.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ audience.summary }}</p>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p style="color: var(--muted); margin-top: 24px;">
    No coding or technical background is needed, unless you ask for an advanced track.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="section" id="formats" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  <span class="eyebrow">Training formats</span>
  <h2>From a single talk to a full programme</h2>
  <p style="color: var(--muted);">Every format can be delivered online or in person, for groups of any size.</p>

  <table class="training-formats">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Format</th>
        <th scope="col">Length</th>
        <th scope="col">Best for</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for format in training.formats %}
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">{{ format.name }}</th>
          <td class="training-formats__length">{{ format.length }}</td>
          <td>{{ format.bestFor }}</td>
        </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 40px;">Add to any format</h3>
  <div class="badges">
    {% for addOn in training.addOns %}<span class="badge">{{ addOn }}</span>{% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="topics" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  <span class="eyebrow">Training topics</span>
  <h2>What your team can learn</h2>
  <p style="max-width: 820px; color: var(--muted);">
    Each topic works as a stand-alone lecture, a workshop or a module in a longer course. Mix and
    match them into your own programme.
  </p>
  <div class="speaking-topics-grid">
    {% for topic in training.topics %}
      <div class="topic-card">
        <div class="topic-icon">{% if loop.index < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ loop.index }}</div>
        <h3>{{ topic.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ topic.summary }}</p>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top: 30px;">
    Don't see your topic? Courses can be built around your own crop, livestock, product, process or
    research area. <a class="text-link" href="{{ training.enquiry }}">Tell me what you need →</a>
  </p>
</section>

<section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
  <h2>From first message to confident team in four steps</h2>
  <div class="speaking-topics-grid training-steps">
    {% for step in training.steps %}
      <div class="topic-card">
        <div class="topic-icon">{{ loop.index }}</div>
        <h3>{{ step.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ step.summary }}</p>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section speaker-creds">
  <h2>Real skills, not just slides</h2>
  <p style="text-align: center; opacity: 0.8; margin-top: -20px;">After the training, participants can:</p>
  <ul class="speaking-list training-outcomes">
    {% for outcome in training.outcomes %}<li>{{ outcome }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="speaking-styles">
    <div class="style-grid">
      <div class="style-text">
        <span class="eyebrow">About your trainer</span>
        <h2>Learn from someone who builds AI for agriculture</h2>
        <p>
          I'm a scientist, founder and educator working where AI meets agriculture. I co-founded
          Petiole, whose platform Petiole Pro uses computer vision to measure plants in the field and
          the lab, and founded <a class="text-link" href="/moomore/">MooMore</a>, AI thermal imaging
          for early lameness detection in dairy cattle — winner of the Innovate UK Women in
          Innovation Award 2026.
        </p>
        <ul class="speaking-list">
          <li>Created the free course <em>{{ awareness.title }}</em>, taken by {{ stats.udemy }} students in {{ stats.countries }} countries</li>
          <li>Writes the AI in Agriculture newsletter for {{ stats.newsletter }} readers on LinkedIn, and the <a class="text-link" href="/books/">AI in Agriculture book series</a></li>
          <li>Speaks at industry events, universities and policy forums — see <a class="text-link" href="/events/">past events</a></li>
          <li>Oxford Farming Conference Inspire Fellow 2026 and LinkedIn Top Voice</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="color: var(--muted);">
          Because I build real AI systems for agriculture, every session is grounded in what actually
          works on farms and in labs, not in theory or sales talk.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="style-visual">
        {{ photo(photos.aiCamp, sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 520px") }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  <span class="eyebrow">Start before we meet</span>
  <h2>Free for everyone on your team, today</h2>
  <p style="max-width: 820px; color: var(--muted);">
    Two courses your people can take on their own, at their own pace, before or after the training.
  </p>
  <div class="grid training-courses">
    <div class="card card--compact">
      <span class="eyebrow" style="font-size: 10px;">AI awareness · Free · Open now</span>
      <h3>{{ awareness.title }}</h3>
      <p>
        {{ awareness.lessons }} video lessons ({{ awareness.length }}), {{ awareness.quizzes }} marked
        quizzes, and a certificate of completion anyone can verify.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="{{ awareness.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Start the free course →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card card--compact">
      <span class="eyebrow" style="font-size: 10px;">AI fluency · In preparation</span>
      <h3>{{ fluency.title }}</h3>
      <p>
        A practical course on briefing AI assistants well — no code, no jargon, with examples from
        farms, trial plots and food businesses throughout.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="{{ fluency.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join the waitlist →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#
  Law and statistics, each with its source named and linked. Every number and
  date here is checked by `npm run check:figures`, weekly in GitHub Actions:
  against aiinagriculture.org, and against the primary source itself. Never
  say or imply that training or a certificate makes an organisation compliant.
#}
<section class="section" id="eu-ai-act" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  <div class="training-law">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">The law</span>
      <h2>Support your EU AI Act AI-literacy duty</h2>
      <p class="lead">{{ training.act.answer }}</p>
      <p>{{ training.act.note }}</p>
      <p class="training-source">
        Sources:
        {% for src in training.act.sources -%}
          <a href="{{ src.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ src.name }}</a>, {{ src.detail }}{% if loop.last %}.{% else %}; {% endif %}
        {% endfor -%}
        This is a summary, not legal advice.
        Last reviewed <time datetime="{{ training.reviewed }}">{{ training.reviewed | readableDate }}</time>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">In the UK</span>
      <h3>Where UK workers are starting from</h3>
      <ul class="training-figures">
        {% for figure in training.figures %}
          <li>
            <strong>{{ figure.value }}</strong>
            <p>{{ figure.text }}</p>
            <p class="training-source"><a href="{{ figure.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ figure.source }}</a></p>
          </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="questions" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
  <span class="eyebrow">Questions, Answered</span>
  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="training-faq">
    {% for item in training.faq %}
      <details class="card card--compact">
        <summary><h3>{{ item.question }}</h3></summary>
        <p>{{ item.answer }}</p>
      </details>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--cta" style="background: var(--accent); color: white; border-radius: var(--radius); text-align: center; margin: 40px 0;">
  <h2 style="color: white;">Ready to build your team's AI skills?</h2>
  <p style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;">
    Tell me about your organisation and what you would like your team to learn. You will get a
    tailored proposal for a lecture, a workshop or a custom programme. Online and on-site delivery
    across the UK and internationally.
  </p>
  <a class="btn" style="background: white; color: var(--accent); margin-top: 20px;" href="{{ training.enquiry }}">Request a proposal</a>
</section>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Service",
      "@id": "{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}#service",
      "name": "AI training for agriculture and agrifood teams",
      "serviceType": "AI literacy and AI fluency training",
      "description": {{ training.definition | dump | safe }},
      "url": "{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}",
      "areaServed": "Worldwide",
      "availableLanguage": "en",
      "provider": { "@type": "Person", "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#person", "name": {{ site.name | dump | safe }} },
      "hasOfferCatalog": {
        "@type": "OfferCatalog",
        "name": "Training formats",
        "itemListElement": [
          {%- for format in training.formats %}
          {
            "@type": "Offer",
            "itemOffered": {
              "@type": "Service",
              "name": {{ format.name | dump | safe }},
              "description": {{ (format.length + ". " + format.bestFor) | dump | safe }}
            }
          }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
          {%- endfor %}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}#faq",
      "mainEntity": [
        {%- for item in training.faq %}
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": {{ item.question | dump | safe }},
          "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ item.answer | dump | safe }} }
        }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
</script>
